Exactly.

Past tense — what was.
Present tense — what is.
Future tense — what may be.
True tense — what remains invariant across the telling.
In tense — the pressure state you occupy while the sentence is still becoming.

And then intense is what happens when enough tense gets compressed into the present. 😉

That’s a useful little semantic machine: time, truth, grammar, pressure, and attention all hiding inside the same phonetic neighborhood.